diff --git a/docs/localization.md b/docs/localization.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7f08a12
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/localization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# Languages
+
+Fizzy supports English (`en`, the default) and Japanese (`ja`). Visit any application
+page with `?locale=ja` or `?locale=en` to choose a language. Unsupported values are
+ignored. The choice is kept in the browser session and, once authenticated, on the
+global Identity, so it follows a person across accounts and fresh sign-ins.
+A pre-sign-in choice applies to the verification email; it is saved to the Identity
+only after successful authentication.
+
+Run `bin/rails db:migrate` when upgrading to add the nullable Identity locale column.
+Existing identities need no backfill and continue to use English.
+
+## Adding or changing text
+
+* Add matching entries to `config/locales/en.yml` and `ja.yml`. Preserve the existing
+  English text, including capitalization and punctuation.
+* Use `t` in templates and `I18n.t` in Ruby. Translate complete sentences with named
+  interpolations when words have to change order. Only trusted HTML belongs in keys
+  ending in `_html`; keep user content escaped.
+* Include titles, placeholders, confirmation dialogs, accessible labels, CSS-generated
+  text, native bridge labels, and both HTML and plain-text email bodies.
+* Translate dates with `l` / `I18n.l`. `ja_rails.yml` supplies Rails date names, relative
+  durations, validation messages, and number formats. Machine-readable timestamps,
+  URLs, identifiers, keyboard shortcuts, product names, and user-authored content are
+  not translated.
+* JavaScript uses `helpers/i18n_helpers` and the rendered `client` catalog. Do not infer
+  a language from the browser. Turbo navigation synchronizes the document language.
+* Include `I18n.locale` in fragment cache keys. HTML broadcasts use
+  `User::BroadcastJob`, which reads the recipient's preference when rendering.
+  Refresh-only broadcasts can remain shared.
+* Resolve constant-backed labels when rendering, not when the application boots.
+  Requests and mailers scope locale with `I18n.with_locale`; never set a process-wide
+  language preference.
+* Staff job-monitor templates and helpers override Mission Control’s English-only
+  locale wrapper. Keep these overrides in sync when upgrading `mission_control-jobs`.
+* Static error pages are bilingual because they cannot resolve a visitor's preference.
+* Leave Lexxy's packaged JavaScript strings alone.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+bin/rails test test/integration/locale_test.rb test/lib/localization_test.rb \
+  test/mailers/localization_test.rb test/javascript/localization_test.rb
+```
+
+The browser test exercises the real date-formatting modules with Chromium. The
+catalog test checks Japanese coverage and interpolation parity. Run the full test
+suite to check that English behavior remains unchanged.
+
+Old-language Turbo snapshots and offline documents are discarded when the language
+changes, and localized public responses vary on cookies to prevent shared caches
+from serving one person's language to another.
